 r←req Submit job;ticket
⍝ Accept a job, start the work in a separate thread, and return a ticket number straight away
⍝ req - the request; job - namespace from the JSON body with
⍝       n        the number to factor: a whole number from 2 to 1E12
⍝       callback the URL to post the result to, e.g. "http://localhost:8082/Result"
⍝       seconds  [optional] how long the work should pretend to take (default: 2 to 4 seconds at random)
⍝ r   - namespace with the ticket number, e.g. {"ticket":17}; HTTP 400 if the job is not valid
 :If 9≠⌊⎕NC'job' ⍝ no request body: job is '' rather than a namespace
     job←⎕NS''
 :EndIf
 :If ~∧/2=⌊job.⎕NC'n' 'callback'
     r←'A job needs "n" and "callback"'
     r req.Fail 400
     →0
 :EndIf
⍝ Check the values too: a bad n would fail later in Work, after the client already has a ticket
 :If ~{(0=≢⍴⍵)∧2|⎕DR ⍵:(⍵=⌊⍵)∧(2≤⍵)∧⍵≤1E12 ⋄ 0}job.n ⍝ a single number (odd ⎕DR), whole, in range
     r←'"n" must be a whole number from 2 to 1E12'
     r req.Fail 400
     →0
 :EndIf
 :If ~{(1=≢⍴⍵)∧0=10|⎕DR ⍵}job.callback ⍝ a character vector
     r←'"callback" must be a URL'
     r req.Fail 400
     →0
 :EndIf
 :Hold 'Ex2Ticket' ⍝ two requests at once must not get the same ticket
     ticket←LastTicket←LastTicket+1
 :EndHold
 Work&ticket job ⍝ & runs Work in a new thread, so we can answer now
 r←⎕NS''
 r.ticket←ticket
⍝ v20: r←(ticket: ticket)
